# libFuzzer dictionary for rpm_headers: the fixed byte patterns of an rpm header list. The reader
# rejects anything that does not start with the 8-byte magic, and then matches five tags and two
# data types as big-endian 32-bit values, so the engine needs these handed over to get past the
# first check and into the field reads.
"\x8e\xad\xe8\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00"
# Tags: NAME 1000, VERSION 1001, RELEASE 1002, EPOCH 1003, ARCH 1022.
"\x00\x00\x03\xe8"
"\x00\x00\x03\xe9"
"\x00\x00\x03\xea"
"\x00\x00\x03\xeb"
"\x00\x00\x03\xfe"
# Data types: INT32 4, STRING 6.
"\x00\x00\x00\x04"
"\x00\x00\x00\x06"
